IMPORT prelude

-- Enlistment Act 1970 (Singapore) -- who is subject to national service (s 2), full-time service (s 12), operationally ready
-- national service (ss 13 to 15), the employer's duties (ss 21 to 23), exit permits (s 32) and offences (ss 4, 33).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/EA1970.txt (amendments to
-- Act 10 of 2024, in force 1 May 2024).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 13 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the liabilities of the serviceman,
-- his employer and his parents. Not encoded: fitness examination detail, mobilised service, regular service, loss of civilian
-- remuneration (s 24), release, postponement and exemption (discretionary), and the regulations.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Enlistment Act 1970 -- service`

§§ `2 -- who is subject to the Act`

-- s 2: "a person who is a citizen of Singapore or a permanent resident thereof and who is not less than 16 years and 6 months of
-- age and not more than 40 years of age", or not more than 50 for officers, senior military experts and designated skilled
-- occupations. (The Act's provisions are written with "he"; liability to register is set by notice under s 3.)
GIVEN `is citizen or PR` IS A BOOLEAN, `age` IS A NUMBER, `is officer or expert` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is subject to the Act` IF
        `is citizen or PR`
    AND `age` AT LEAST 16.5
    AND (IF `is officer or expert` THEN `age` AT MOST 50 ELSE `age` AT MOST 40)

§§ `12 -- full-time service`

-- s 12(1): full-time service "not exceeding 2 years", except that a person promoted above LANCE-CORPORAL (or equivalent), or selected
-- for or undergoing officer training, serves "not exceeding 2 years and 6 months". (2): a later reduction in rank does not reduce
-- the liability.
GIVEN `promoted above lance-corporal or selected for officer training` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum full-time service in months` MEANS
    IF `promoted above lance-corporal or selected for officer training` THEN 30 ELSE 24

§§ `13 to 15 -- operationally ready national service`

-- s 14(1)(b): not more than 40 DAYS a year in aggregate (more if authorised). s 15(1): (a) a continuous period spanning two years
-- counts in the first; (b) up to 4 hours counts as HALF a day; (c) 4 to 24 hours as ONE day; (d) over 24 hours, every calendar day
-- counts, including the first and last. (2): 18 to 24 hours spread over 2 calendar days counts as 2 days.
GIVEN `hours` IS A NUMBER, `calendar days touched` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days of service counted` MEANS
    IF `hours` AT MOST 4 THEN 0.5
    ELSE IF `hours` GREATER THAN 24 THEN `calendar days touched`
         ELSE IF `hours` AT LEAST 18 AND `calendar days touched` EQUALS 2 THEN 2 ELSE 1

§§ `21 to 23 -- the employer`

-- s 21(1): an employer who employed the serviceman for at least 6 MONTHS continuously before the call-up must reinstate him at the end
-- of service; (3) not if he was employed only for an agreed fixed term.
-- s 22(1): no employer may dismiss a person "solely or mainly" because of a service liability, unless (e) called up for full-time
-- service and employed for a fixed term. (3): where service "caused or CONTRIBUTED to" the dismissal, it is deemed the reason
-- "unless the employer proves" otherwise. (4): $2,000 or 6 months, and compensation of up to 3 months' remuneration.
-- s 23: the employer must grant leave of absence for service -- $5,000 or 3 years.
GIVEN `months employed before call-up` IS A NUMBER, `fixed-term only` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employer must reinstate` IF
    `months employed before call-up` AT LEAST 6 AND (NOT `fixed-term only`)

GIVEN `service contributed to the dismissal` IS A BOOLEAN, `employer proved an unconnected reason` IS A BOOLEAN, `fixed-term full-time call-up` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the dismissal is unlawful under section 22` IF
    `service contributed to the dismissal` AND (NOT `employer proved an unconnected reason`) AND (NOT `fixed-term full-time call-up`)

GIVEN `monthly pay` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum compensation for unlawful dismissal` MEANS
    `monthly pay` TIMES 3

§§ `32 -- exit permits`

-- s 32(1): a person subject to the Act, or a "relevant child", must not leave or remain outside Singapore without a valid exit permit;
-- (2) must return before it expires. (5): a "relevant child" is a citizen or PR aged at least 13 but under 16 years and 6 months.
-- (3): the child commits an offence ($2,000); (4): so does EACH PARENT, "within or outside Singapore" ($2,000).
GIVEN `age` IS A NUMBER, `is citizen or PR` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is a relevant child` IF
    `is citizen or PR` AND `age` AT LEAST 13 AND `age` LESS THAN 16.5

GIVEN `the child overstayed without a permit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `each parent commits an offence` IF
    `the child overstayed without a permit`

§§ `4, 33 -- offences`

-- s 4(2): failing without lawful excuse to register -- $10,000 or 3 years; (3) then $50 a day after the date the court sets.
-- s 33: failing to comply with a notice, failing to fulfil a liability, fraudulently obtaining exemption, acting to evade service,
-- giving false information, or abetting any of these -- "any person within or OUTSIDE Singapore" -- $10,000 or 3 years.
GIVEN `days late after the court's date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the continuing fine for not registering` MEANS
    `days late after the court's date` TIMES 50
